dialogue joined_wild
title: Things that grow
trigger: Joined wild
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  The newcomer from the Wild hasn't come near the fire. They sit in the long grass at the camp's edge, where a small red flower has opened between two stones.
  * You followed the caravan for days. I hoped you'd come in. -> walked
    if: TrustAtLeast $hero 15
  * You've joined us. Come sit where it's warm, and talk with me. -> signed

node walked hero
  Animals follow a herd before they join it. You have to see if the herd eats its weak ones. Yours doesn't.
  -> grow

node signed hero
  Warm is fine. Walls are not. If you want me close, don't put a roof over me.
  -> grow

node grow hero
  Out in the Wild, things grow where the sky's pieces fell. Red things, in the white. The Choir says they're poison. They're not. They're just alive.
  -> listen

node listen commander
  The red flower turns, very slightly, toward the orb on the Commander's belt.
  * I'd like to see where they grow. Will you show me? -> show
    do: AddTrust $hero 8
  * I don't understand any of it yet. I'll listen. -> ears
    do: AddTrust $hero 5
  * Whatever's growing out there, it isn't safe. Stay close to camp. -> camp
    do: AddTrust $hero -5

node show hero
  You'd come? Most people want to burn it. Yes. When the moon's right. You have to be quiet, though.
  -> touched

node ears hero
  Good. Listening is the first thing the beasts teach you. Talking is the last, and most people never get there.
  -> touched

node camp hero
  Safe. The white things in the Choir's halls are safe. Nothing grows on them at all. I'll stay close, but I won't stay tame.
  -> touched

node touched hero
  Some of us have been touched by it. Changed a little. The Choir calls us Bloom-touched like it's a sickness. Does it scare you?
  -> answer

node answer commander
  The wild child's eyes catch the firelight and hold it, a shade too red.
  * No. You're one of us now, changed or not. -> ours
    do: AddTrust $hero 8
  * A little. But I'd rather understand it than fear it. -> honest
    do: AddTrust $hero 6
  * It might. Tell me if it ever changes you further. -> further
    do: AddTrust $hero 2

node ours hero
  One of us. The beasts will like hearing that. I'll tell them tonight.

node honest hero
  Scared and still sitting here. That's how a good tamer starts, Commander.

node further hero
  I'll tell you. I tell everyone I trust when something new grows. You're on the list now.
